        "original_id": "32fbcc0b-9400-5227-a903-ca5d5c1d28df",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Black and White Ball\n- People: Truman Capote, Katharine Graham\n- Organizations: The Washington Post\n- Places: Plaza Hotel, New York City\n- Works: Personal History, Pulitzer Prize\n\nFacts:\n- Katharine Meyer Graham was born on June 16, 1917, and she was an American publisher.\n- The Black and White Ball was a masquerade ball held on November 28, 1966, at the Plaza Hotel in New York City.\n- Truman Capote hosted the Black and White Ball in honor of The Washington Post publisher Katharine Graham.\n- Katharine Graham's memoir Personal History won the Pulitzer Prize in 1998.\n- Katharine Meyer Graham died on July 17, 2001.",
